9-8469-5e83-8243-caaa61ac2eb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-87151" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The number of heads obtained when a coin is flipped twice\n- The height of a randomly selected person, measured in meters\n- The concentration, in grams per cubic centimeter, of glucose in a person's bloodstream" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073533/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $0,1,2,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $(0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the real interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87151/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87151"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "42455bf1-f82b-5934-a543-60915b3f6f97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "38e359bd-12c7-5e88-9aec-6cd31e050c5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "def0abb8-e7f1-5004-ae17-5155299788f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "ebbfc6e2-fd3f-5436-aae4-e645605e75f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "57c27147-63ce-52f6-b6df-a82497bd3f3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac58a6b3-2ab2-5915-a9c6-1cbb3af9c684" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126057/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer-field/choices ["q-126057/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-126057/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-126057/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-126057/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-126057/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126057" :question/id #uuid "b9a5bb55-99d4-5b06-9d25-2f1d72810107" :question/math-academy-id "q-126057" :question/problem "Which of the following are continuous random variables?\n\n- The number obtained when throwing a die\n- The weight, measured in grams, of sugar in a bowl\n- The speed limit on a certain road" :question/worked-solution "A random variable is a variable whose value is determined by the outcome of a trial or experiment. A *continuous* random variable is a random variable whose possible values are represented by an interval of real numbers.\n\nCommon examples of continuous random variables are shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073533/assets/05e3d893f6c069dce5b51dc7d9fa5830b44bca58fa071009548fde20ebe92c19.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I does *not* describe a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, but its possible values are the integers $1,2,3,4,5,6,$ which do not correspond to an interval of real numbers.\n\n- Statement II describes a continuous random variable. Its value is determined by the result of an experiment, and its possible values correspond to the interval $[0,\\infty ).$\n\n- Statement III does *not* describe a continuous random variable. The speed limit on a certain road is not the outcome of a trial or experiment.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126057/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ee39554-fd77-5e90-baa8-f9320ffc3398"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126057"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126061/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "1b8f4e06-e39b-577f-a7cb-bd4906134ff2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126061/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "9d22ce36-5e84-5c66-be47-bed6d